<main>
  <section class="page-hero page-hero--mint" id="overview">
    <div class="wrap page-hero__grid">
      <div class="page-hero__copy reveal">
        <span class="ey">Customers</span>
        <h1>Evaluate the buyer workflow before you commit.</h1>
        <p class="lead">Public customer stories are not published yet. You can still evaluate the verified product workflow, connection model and onboarding questions that matter to your buyer requirement.</p>
        <div class="page-hero__actions"><a class="btn pri" href="/book-demo/">Discuss your requirement &rarr;</a><a class="btn secbtn" href="#evaluation">What to review &darr;</a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-visual reveal" aria-label="Customer evaluation path"><div class="hero-visual__label"><span>PunchOut Central</span><b>Evaluate</b></div><div class="visual-flow"><div class="visual-step is-accent"><i>01</i><span><strong>Buyer requirement</strong><small>Procurement system and protocol</small></span><em>Define</em></div><div class="visual-step is-lavender"><i>02</i><span><strong>Store connection</strong><small>Shopify catalog and access</small></span><em>Map</em></div><div class="visual-step is-peach"><i>03</i><span><strong>Test transaction</strong><small>Cart, PO and order</small></span><em>Validate</em></div></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec" id="evaluation"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">Verified product evidence</span><h2>Start with the parts of the workflow we can describe precisely.</h2><p class="lead">The verified product playbook describes the following operating model. Customer names, outcomes and independent proof are intentionally not inferred from it.</p></div><div class="feature-grid">
    <article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">01</span><h3>Existing Shopify store</h3><p>Use Shopify or Shopify Plus as the supplier catalog rather than creating a separate PunchOut storefront.</p><p><a href="/integrations/shopify/">Review Shopify connectivity &rarr;</a></p></article>
    <article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">02</span><h3>Buyer-specific access</h3><p>Assign the relevant store and collections or catalog access to each enterprise buyer connection.</p><p><a href="/solutions/one-store-multiple-buyers/">See the shared-store model &rarr;</a></p></article>
    <article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">03</span><h3>End-to-end transaction</h3><p>Follow PunchOut Started, Cart Returned, Buyer Approved, PO Received, Store Order Created and Invoice Generated.</p><p><a href="/platform/transactions/">Explore transaction tracking &rarr;</a></p></article>
    <article class="feature-card reveal"><span class="feature-card__icon">04</span><h3>Buyer-specific onboarding</h3><p>Confirm the procurement system, cXML or OCI expectation, catalog scope, test path and order documents with the buyer.</p><p><a href="/documentation/">Read setup documentation &rarr;</a></p></article>
  </div></div></section>

  <section class="sec soft" id="questions"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head reveal"><span class="ey">Before a case study exists</span><h2>Bring evidence you can actually verify.</h2><p class="lead">For a buyer review, ask for the current requirements rather than relying on a logo wall or an unqualified success claim.</p></div><div class="simple-steps">
    <article class="simple-step reveal"><span class="simple-step__num">01</span><h3>Identify the buyer</h3><p>Record the procurement platform, buyer contact, protocol expectation and test environment.</p></article>
    <article class="simple-step reveal"><span class="simple-step__num">02</span><h3>Map the store</h3><p>Choose the Shopify store, collections and buyer-specific catalog access required.</p></article>
    <article class="simple-step reveal"><span class="simple-step__num">03</span><h3>Test the handoff</h3><p>Validate session launch, cart return, approval, PO receipt and Shopify order creation.</p></article>
    <article class="simple-step reveal"><span class="simple-step__num">04</span><h3>Document the result</h3><p>Keep the buyer-approved test outcome and operating details for the internal team.</p></article>
  </div></div></section>

  <section class="page-cta"><div class="wrap reveal"><span class="ey">No invented proof</span><h2>Review the real buyer requirement with the team.</h2><p class="lead">Bring the procurement system, Shopify store and catalog scope for a focused conversation.</p><div class="page-hero__actions"><a class="btn pri" href="/book-demo/">Request a demo &rarr;</a><a class="btn secbtn" href="/pricing/">Compare plans</a></div></div></section>
</main>
